    <string name="tour_start">Get started</string>
    <string name="tour_1_title">Your homelab on one screen</string>
    <string name="tour_1_body">All your services together, grouped and colour-coded. Each
        one opens right here, in its own tab, without leaving the app.</string>
    <string name="tour_2_title">Add them however you like</string>
    <string name="tour_2_body">Scan your network for whatever answers, bring in the panel
        you already use — Homer, Homarr, Heimdall — or add them one by one.</string>
    <string name="tour_3_title">At home and away</string>
    <string name="tour_3_body">Each machine can have two addresses: the one on your network
        and the one over the VPN. The panel uses whichever fits.\n\nRemember to pick your
        WiFi network in Settings › Security.</string>
    <string name="tour_4_title">Send links to your downloads</string>
    <string name="tour_4_body">An ed2k, a magnet or a torrent you tap anywhere can be sent
        to your own aMule, qBittorrent, Transmission or SABnzbd.</string>
    <string name="tour_5_title">Your data stays here</string>
    <string name="tour_5_body">Passwords are stored encrypted on the phone and the app
        talks only to your machines. No accounts, no analytics, no cloud.</string>
    <string name="tour_6_title">The only permission asked for</string>
    <string name="tour_6_body">Location, and only to read the name of your WiFi: it is the
        one thing Android accepts for that. Your position is never looked up, never stored
        and never leaves this phone.\n\nWithout it the panel cannot tell which network it
        is on, nor your home from another using the same addresses.</string>

    <string name="ask_network_title">Almost there</string>
    <string name="ask_network_body">Tell the panel which WiFi is yours, so it does not
        mistake your home for any other network. One tap in Settings › Security.</string>
